Read AGENTS.md in the repo root before making changes. It is the canonical
instruction file for this repository and applies to every AI agent working
here, Windsurf included.

Highlights (full detail is in AGENTS.md):

- Packages are organized into 6 ESLint-enforced tiers
  (packages/eslint-config/boundaries.js). A package may only import from
  strictly lower tiers; api and web (tier 5) never import each other.
- Every request/response shape is a TypeBox schema in packages/contracts,
  imported by both backend and frontend. Never hand-write a duplicate type.
- Backend flow: contracts -> repository (Drizzle queries only) -> service
  (business rules + auth) -> controller (thin, wires Elysia context). Row-to-
  DTO mapping happens only in <domain>.mapper.ts, with every field assigned
  explicitly (never spread a row into a response).
- Cursor-based pagination everywhere; never offset/page.
- Soft deletes only on catalogue data (anime, episodes) — filter on
  deletedAt, never hard-delete; progress/comments/ratings reference these
  rows.
- Redis keys always go through redisKeys.* in packages/redis/src/keys.ts,
  never a raw template string (it silently escapes the namespace prefix).
- Do not restart, kill, or start the API/web dev servers without asking the
  user first — they run these themselves. Verify fixes against the already-
  running stack instead (curl, direct DB/Redis query).
- bun --watch on the API does not reliably pick up edits in sibling
  workspace packages (e.g. packages/auth) — a manual restart is often needed,
  which is the user's call, not yours to make unprompted.

Package-level READMEs (e.g. packages/shared/README.md) take precedence over
AGENTS.md for anything specific to that package.
